git by digit:\n\nFirst number: 566,677\n\nDigits from right to left:\n\nPosition 1 (ones):7\n\n2 (tens):7\n\n3 (hundreds):6\n\n4 (thousands):6\n\n5 (ten thousands):6\n\n6 (hundred thousands):5\n\nSecond number:992,307\n\nDigits from right to left:\n\nPosition 1 (ones):7\n\n2 (tens):0\n\n3 (hundreds):3\n\n4 (thousands):2\n\n5 (ten thousands):9\n\n6 (hundred thousands):9\n\nSo adding each column:\n\nPosition 1 (ones):7+7=14 \u2192 4, carryover 1.\n\nPosition 2 (tens):7+0 +1=8 \u2192 8, no carryover.\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds):6+3=9 \u21929, no carryover.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):6 (from first number) +2 (from second)=8 \u21928, no carryover.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):6 (first) +9 (second)=15 \u21925, carryover 1.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):5 (first) +9 (second)=14, plus carryover 1 \u219215. So 5 in hundred thousands, carryover 1 to millions.\n\nThen the millions place: the carryover 1. So the total is 1,5 (million), then 5 (hundred thousand?), wait:\n\nWait, the digits would be:\n\nMillions place: 1\n\nHundred thousands:5\n\nTen thousands:5\n\nThousands:8\n\nHundreds:9\n\nTens:8\n\nOnes:4\n\nSo combining, 1,558,984. Yes, that's correct. So the answer is 1,558,984. Alright, that seems right.\n</think>\n\n",
