ens, and 5 in the ones. Wait, hold on, let me check that again. Maybe I messed up the places.\n\nWait, let me go step by step again carefully. Let me write each digit position:.\n\nLet's line them up:.\n\n      6 3 8 7 2 8.\n    + 4 6 0 5 2 7.\n    ----------------.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\nOnes: 8 +7 =15. Write 5, carryover 1.\n\nTens: 2 +2 =4, plus 1 is 5. Write 5.\n\nHundreds:7 +5 =12. Write 2, carryover 1.\n\nThousands:8 +0 =8, plus 1 =9. Write 9.\n\nTen-thousands:3 +6 =9. Write 9.\n\nHundred-thousands:6 +4 =10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nSince there's a carryover after the hundred thousands, that adds a new digit at the millions place: 1.\n\nSo putting all together: 1 (million), 0 (hundred thousand), 9 (ten thousand), 9 (thousand), 2 (hundred), 5 (ten), 5 (one). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
