messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the addition problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of <<number1>> and <<number2>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n1. The ones place: <<digit1>>\n2. The tens place: <<digit2>>\n<<other digits>>\nAnswer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 879858 and 936138?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\nOkay, I need to add 879,858 and 936,138. Let me write them down to make it easier.\n\nStarting with the ones place: 8 + 8 is 16. Hmm, I'll write down 6 and carry over 1. .\n\nNext, the tens place: 5 + 3 is 8, plus the carried 1 makes 9. No carryover here.\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 8 + 1 is 9. Still nothing to carry.\n\nNow the thousands place: 9 + 6 equals 15. So I put 5 and carry over 1.\n\nTens of thousands place: 7 + 3 is 10, plus the 1 makes 11. Write 1 and carry 1 again.\n\nFinally, the hundred thousands place: 8 + 9 is 17, plus the carried 1 gives 18. .\n\nPutting all together, it should be 1,816, 0.. wait, let me check again. Wait, maybe I messed up the places. Let me recount each digit step by step carefully.\n\nWait, let me align the numbers properly:.\n\n  879858.\n+ 936138.\n----------.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 8 + 8 = 16. Write 6, carry 1.\n\nTens: 5 + 3 = 8 + 1 (carry) = 9. No carry.\n\nHundreds: 8 + 1 = 9. Still 9, no carry.\n\nThousands: 9 (from first number) + 6 (from second) = 15. Write 5, carry 1.\n\nTen-thousands place: 7 (from first number, since 879,858 has 7 in the ten-thousands place?) Wait, hold on, maybe I messed up the digit positions.\n\nWait, let me write the numbers digit by digit:.\n\nFirst number: 879,858 is 8 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 8 (ones).\n\nSecond number: 936,138 is 9 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 8 (ones).\n\nSo adding each column:.\n\nOnes: 8+8=16. 6, carryover 1.\n\nTens:5+3=8 +1=9. No carry.\n\nHundreds:8 (from first) +1 (from second) =9. No carry.\n\nThousands:9 (first) +6 (second) =15. So 5, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands:7 (first) +3 (second) =10, plus 1 carried is 11. So write 1 and carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands:8 +9 =17 plus 1 carried is 18. .\n\nSo putting all together: 1 (from the million place) 8 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 5 (thousands), 9 (hundreds),9 (tens),6 (ones). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
