ens), 8 (ones).\n\n619,120 is 6 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 0 (ones).\n\nAdding them:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes place: 8 + 0 = 8. Write 8.\n\nTens place: 8 + 2 = 10. Write 0, carry over 1.\n\nHundreds place: 1 + 1 = 2, plus the carried 1 makes 3. Write 3.\n\nThousands place: 8 + 9 = 17. Write 7, carry over 1.\n\nTen-thousands place: 2 + 1 = 3, plus the carried 1 makes 4. Write 4.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 4 + 6 = 10. Write 10. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
