 number) and 9 (second number) plus the carryover from thousands place (which was 1). So 8+9=17 plus 1 is 18. So the digit here is 8, carryover 1. Then hundred thousands place: 2+1 +1 =4. So yes, that's correct.\n\nTherefore the final answer should be 485,616.\n\nBut let me do a direct addition to confirm once more:\n\n289,565\n\n+196,051\n\nAdd units: 5+1=6.\n\nTens:6+5=11, write 1, carry 1.\n\nHundreds:5+0 +1=6.\n\nThousands:9+6=15, write 5 carry 1.\n\nTen-thousands:8+9 +1=18, so 8 and carry 1.\n\nHundred thousands:2+1 +1=4.\n\nSo indeed 485,616. Okay, confident now.\n</think>\n\n",
