housands place: 8\n\n- Hundreds place: 1\n\n- Tens place: 0\n\n- Ones place: 4\n\nWait, no, that can't be right. Wait 418,104:\n\nDigits: 4 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 4 (ones). Yes, that's correct. So positions are:\n\nHundred thousands: 4\n\nTen thousands: 1\n\nThousands:8\n\nHundreds:1\n\nTens:0\n\nOnes:4\n\nSecond number:397,962\n\nBreaking down:\n\nHundred thousands:3\n\nTen thousands:9\n\nThousands:7\n\nHundreds:9\n\nTens:6\n\nOnes:2\n\nSo when adding, the thousands place is 8 (first number) and 7 (second). So adding those gives 15 plus the carryover 1 (from the hundreds place addition) makes 16. Wait, but the hundreds place was first number 1 and second 9, so that was 10, leading to carryover 1. So that's correct.\n\nThen ten thousands place: first number's ten thousands digit is 1 and second's is 9. So 1+9=10 plus the carryover 1 (from thousands place addition) gives 11, so 1 and carryover 1. Then the hundred thousands:4 +3 +1 (carryover) =8. That's right. So the total is 816,066. \n\nI think that's correct. I can't see any mistakes here. So the answer should be 816,066.\n"]
