digit, the sum might be a seven-digit number here. Let me check again.\n\nWait, actually, let me go through each step again to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nStarting over:.\n\nAligning the numbers:.\n\n```.\n  470434.\n+ 581434.\n----------.\n```.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes place: 4 + 4 = 8 ✔️.\n\nTens: 3 + 3 = 6 ✔️.\n\nHundreds: 4 + 4 = 8 ✔️.\n\nThousands: 0 + 1 = 1 ✔️.\n\nTen thousands: 7 (from first number) + 8 (from second) = 15. So write 5, carry over 1. ✔️.\n\nHundred thousands: 4 + 5 = 9, plus the carried 1 makes 10. So yes, that's 10. So the hundred thousands place becomes 0, and we have to carry over 1 to the millions place. Since there are no more digits, that carried 1 becomes the new digit in the millions place. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
