      "text": "1,297,488?\n\nWait, let me check that again step by step to be sure. Maybe I made a mistake in the places.\n\nWait, let's do it again step by step systematically:\n\nLet me write the numbers vertically:\n\n    8 2 5 3 0 3\n  + 4 7 2 1 8 5\n  ----------------\nStarting from the right (ones place):\n\nOnes: 3 + 5 = 8 \u2192 8\n\nTens: 0 + 8 = 8 \u2192 8\n\nHundreds: 3 + 1 = 4 \u2192 4\n\nThousands: 5 + 2 = 7? Wait, hold on. Wait, maybe I misaligned the digits earlier. Let me check the positions again.\n\nWait, perhaps I messed up the place values. Let me break down each digit properly. Let me note each digit's place:\n\nFirst number: 825,303. Breaking down each digit from right to left:\n\n- Ones: 3\n\n- Tens: 0\n\n- Hundreds: 3\n\n- Thousands: 5\n\n- Ten-thousands: 2\n\n- Hundred-thousands: 8\n\nSecond number: 472,185.\n\nBreaking down similarly:\n\n- Ones: 5\n\n- Tens: 8\n\n- Hundreds: 1\n\n- Thousands: 2\n\n- Ten-thousands: 7\n\n- Hundred-thousands: 4\n\nWait, so when adding, the thousands place is 5 (from first number) and 2 (from second). 5 + 2 = 7. Wait, but earlier I thought that was 5 +8? Wait, that must have been my mistake. Let me correct that.\n\nWait, I think I mixed up the thousands and ten-thousands places earlier. Let me redo the addition step by step carefully:\n\nStarting over:\n\nOnes place: 3 (from first number) +5 (second) =8. Correct.\n\nTens place: 0 +8 =8. Correct.\n\nHundreds place: 3 +1 =4. Correct.\n\nThousands place:5 (from first) +2 (from second) =7. Wait, so that's 7, no carry-over here. So why did I previously think 5+8? Oh, because maybe I misread the second number's thousands place. Let me confirm the second number again.\n\nWait second number is 472,185. So the digits are:\n\nHundred thousands:4,\n\nTen thousands:7,\n\nThousands:2,\n\nHundreds:1,\n\nTens:8,\n\nOnes:5.\n\nYes. So thousands place is 2. So 5+2=7, no carry-over. That was my mistake earlier. So then moving to ten-thousands place:\n\nFirst number's ten-thousands digit is 2, second's is7. So 2 +7 =9. No carry-over here. So ten-thousands is 9.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 8 +4 =12. So that's 2 with a carry-over of 1 to the millions place. So the sum would be 1 (million) 2 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 8 (ones). So putting together: 1,297,488.\n\nWait, but when I first thought I had a mistake in thousands place, but actually I had messed up in my first calculation. Wait let me confirm again step by step:\n\nLet me write them vertically with each digit:\n\nFirst number: 8 (hundred thousand), 2 (ten thousand),5 (thousand),3 (hundred),0 (ten),3 (one).\n\nSecond number:4 (hundred thousand),7 (ten thousand),2 (thousand),1 (hundred),8 (ten),5 (one).\n\nAdding each column:\n\nOnes:3+5=8\n\nTens:0+8=8\n\nHundreds:3+1=4\n\nThousands:5+2=7\n\nTen-thousands:2+7=9\n\nHundred-thousands:8+4=12.\n\nSo the sum is 12 in the hundred thousands place? Wait, that can't be. Wait, the hundred thousands place digits add to 8+4=12, so that's 2 in that place and carry over 1 to the millions place. So the total is 1,297,488.\n\nYes, that's correct. So my initial mistake was when I thought the thousands place was 5+8, but actually the thousands digit of the second number is 2, not 8. So the correct total is 1,297,488. Let me verify with another method, perhaps adding the numbers in parts.\n\nAlternatively, adding 825,303 + 400,000 = 1,225,303. Then add 72,185 (since 472,185 -400,000 =72,185). So 1,225,303 +72,185.\n\nAdding 1,225,303 +70,000 = 1,295,303. Then +2,185: 1,295,303 +2,000=1,297,303, then +185 gives 1,297,488. Same result. So that checks out.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 1,297,488.\n</think>\n\n",
