lace and carry over 1 to the millions place. Wait a second, but the original numbers are both six digits, so adding them might result in a seven-digit number. Let me check again.\n\nWait, let me go step by step again to make sure I didn't make a mistake. Maybe I messed up the places. Let me write them out aligned:.\n\n  835,348.\n+ 835,341.\n----------.\n\nBreaking it down digit by digit from right to left (ones to higher places):.\n\nOnes: 8 + 1 = 9 ✔️.\n\nTens: 4 + 4 = 8 ✔️.\n\nHundreds: 3 + 3 = 6 ✔️.\n\nThousands: 5 + 5 = 10. So write 0, carry over 1. ✔️.\n\nTen-thousands: 3 (from first number) + 3 (from second) + 1 (carry) = 7 ✔️.\n\nHundred-thousands: 8 + 8 = 16. So here, the hundred-thousands place would be 6, and carry over 1 to the millions place. Since there are no more digits, the carried 1 becomes the new millions digit. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
