as 6. 2 + 6 = 8, plus the carried-over 1 gives 9. So that's the hundred-thousands place. .\n\nWait, let me check if there are any more digits. The first number is 223806, which is six digits, and the second is 696963, also six digits. So we've covered all places. Let me write out the sum step by step to make sure I didn't miss anything.\n\nWait a second, maybe I should go through each digit again carefully to avoid mistakes. Let me start over with the addition:.\n\nAligning the numbers:.\n\n  223806.\n+ 696963.\n----------.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones place):.\n\n6 (from 223806) + 3 (from 696963) = 9. Write down 9.\n\nTens place: 0 + 6 = 6. Write down 6.\n\nHundreds place: 8 + 9 = 17. Write down 7, carry over 1.\n\nThousands place: 3 + 6 = 9, plus the carried 1 is 10. Write down 0, carry over 1.\n\nTen-thousands place: 2 + 9 = 11, plus the carried 1 is 12. Write down 2, carry over 1.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 2 + 6 = 8, plus the carried 1 is 9. Write down 9. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
