 down 4 here and carry over 1 to the next higher place.\n\nNow the hundred-thousands place: 3 (from first number) + 9 (from second number) plus the carried-over 1 equals 13. So that's 3 in the hundred-thousands place and a carry-over of 1 to the millions place. Since there are no more digits, that 1 becomes a 1 in the millions place. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
