t 4 (thousands):8.\n\nDigit 5 (ten thousands):8.\n\nDigit 6 (hundred thousands):7.\n\nSecond number:563,977:.\n\nDigit 1 (ones):7.\n\nDigit 2 (tens):7.\n\nDigit 3 (hundreds):9.\n\nDigit 4 (thousands):3.\n\nDigit 5 (ten thousands):6.\n\nDigit 6 (hundred thousands):5.\n\nAdding each column:.\n\nOnes place: 0 +7 =7. Write 7.\n\nTens:5 +7 =12. Write 2, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds:7 +9 =16, plus 1 =17. Write 7, carryover 1.\n\nThousands:8 (from first number) +3 (from second) =11, plus 1 =12. Write 2, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands:8 +6 =14, plus 1=15. Write 5, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands:7 +5 =12, plus 1=13. Write 3, carryover 1.\n\nMillions place: the carried over 1. So the digits from right to left are 7,2,7,2,5,3,1. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
