it:2,\n\nTens digit:7,\n\nOnes digit:8.\n\nSo putting all together: 1 (million), 1 (hundred thousand), 6 (ten thousand), 5 (thousand), 2 (hundred), 7 (ten), 8 (one). So that's 1,165,278. But in my first calculation, I thought it was 1,165,288. So I must have made an error in the first addition. Let me check again the breakdown method:\n\n405,016 + 760,262.\n\nLet me add them as:\n\n405,016 + 700,000 = 1,105,016\n\nThen add 60,000: 1,105,016 +60,000 = 1,165,016\n\nThen add 200: 1,165,016 + 200 = 1,165,216\n\nThen add 60: 1,165,216 +60 =1,165,276\n\nThen add 2: 1,165,276 +2 =1,165,278.\n\nYes, that's correct. So my initial first method had a mistake in the tens place? Wait no, let me see.\n\nWait, in the first method, I thought the tens place was 1+6=7. The first number's tens digit is 1 (from 405,016 which is ...016, so the tens digit is 1), and the second number's tens digit is 6 (from 760,262 which ends with 262, so tens digit is 6). 1+6=7, so that's correct. So the tens digit is 7. Then the hundreds digit is 0+2=2, thousands is 5+0=5, ten thousands is 0+6=6, hundred thousands is 4+7=11. So the sum is 1,165,278. So my first calculation was wrong because I thought the answer was 1,165,288. Probably added an extra 10 somewhere. So the correct answer is 1,165,278.\n\nHmm, so I need to make sure. Let me do the addition another way, perhaps column-wise with the carry-over:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:6+2=8. Write 8.\n\nTens:1+6=7. Write 7.\n\nHundreds:0+2=2. Write 2.\n\nThousands:5+0=5. Write 5.\n\nTen thousands:0+6=6. Write 6.\n\nHundred thousands:4+7=11. Write 1 and carry over 1 to the millions place.\n\nSince there's no millions place in the original numbers, the carried 1 becomes the millions digit. So the digits are:\n\nMillions:1\n\nHundred thousands:1 (from 11)\n\nTen thousands:6\n\nThousands:5\n\nHundreds:2\n\nTens:7\n\nOnes:8.\n\nSo that gives 1,165,278. Yes, that's correct. So the final answer should be 1,165,278. I must have made an addition mistake in my initial first calculation when I thought it was 288. Probably added the tens and hundreds wrong. Okay, so the correct answer is 1,165,278.\n"] 22%|##1       | 108/500 [1:10:12<5:33:40, 51.07s/it]
