 (tens), 9 (ones). So the number is 838,489. That's correct.\n\nHmm, so I think the answer is correct. Maybe I can use another approach, like adding the numbers as whole numbers:\n\n635,068 + 200,000 = 835,068.\n\nThen add 3,421: 835,068 + 3,000 = 838,068; then +421 = 838,489. Yep, same result. Okay, so I feel confident that the answer is 838,489.\n</think>\n\n",
