. Let me write the numbers properly:.\n\nWait, let me check the alignment again. Let's write both numbers with commas for clarity:.\n\n149,744 is 1 (hundred thousand), 4 (ten thousand), 9 (thousand), 7 (hundred), 4 (ten), 4 (one).\n\n421,269 is 4 (hundred thousand), 2 (ten thousand), 1 (thousand), 2 (hundred), 6 (ten), 9 (one).\n\nSo when adding:.\n\nHundred thousands: 1 +4 =5.\n\nTen thousands:4 +2=6.\n\nThousands:9 +1=10.\n\nHundreds:7 +2=9.\n\nTens:4 +6=10.\n\nOnes:4+9=13.\n\nWait, but when adding column by column starting from the right, let's do it properly:.\n\nLet me write the numbers vertically:.\n\n      1 4 9 7 4 4.\n    + 4 2 1 2 6 9.\n    ---------------.\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\n4 +9 =13. Write 3, carryover 1.\n\nTens place: 4 +6 =10, plus 1 is 11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds place:7 +2 =9, plus 1 is 10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place:9 (from first number) +1 (from second) =10, plus 1 carried over is 11. So write 1, carryover 1.\n\nTen-thousands place:4 +2 =6, plus 1 carried over is 7. Write 7, no carryover.\n\nHundred-thousands place:1 +4 =5. Write 5.\n\nPutting all together: 5 (hundred thousand), 7 (ten thousand), 1 (thousand), 0 (hundred), 1 (ten), 3 (one). So that's 570,113?.\n\nWait, wait, now I'm confused because earlier I thought 570,013 but now after rechecking, the thousands place after adding 9+1+1 (carry) is 11, so the thousands digit would be 1 and carryover to the ten-thousands. Let me go step by step again:.\n\nLet me list each digit position with their place values:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes place:.\nFirst number: 4.\nSecond number:9.\nSum:13 → 3, carryover 1.\n\nTens place:.\nFirst number:4.\nSecond number:6.\nSum:4+6=10 +1 (carry) =11 → 1, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds place:.\nFirst number:7.\nSecond number:2.\nSum:7+2=9 +1 (carry)=10 → 0, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place:.\nFirst number:9.\nSecond number:1.\nSum:9+1=10 +1 (carry)=11 → 1, carryover 1.\n\nTen-thousands place:.\nFirst number:4.\nSecond number:2.\nSum:4+2=6 +1 (carry)=7 → 7, no carryover.\n\nHundred-thousands place:.\nFirst number:1.\nSecond number:4.\nSum:1+4=5 →5.\n\nSo combining all the digits from right to left:.\n\nOnes:3, Tens:1, Hundreds:0, Thousands:1, Ten-thousands:7, Hundred-thousands:5.\n\nSo the number is 5 (hundred thousand), 7 (ten thousand), 1 (thousand), 0 (hundred), 1 (ten), 3 (one). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
