 1 in the hundred thousands place and carry over 1 to the millions place. Since there are no other digits in the millions place except the carried over 1, so that becomes the millions digit. .\n\nSo the total would be 1 (million), 1 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 5 (ones). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
