n the millions place is that 1.\n\nSo the total is 1,928,442.\n\nWait, but let me add them numerically to confirm:\n\n935,817 + 992,625.\n\nLet me compute 935,817 + 900,000 = 1,835,817. Then subtract the difference: 992,625 is 92,625 less than 992,625 + 900,000? Wait no. Alternatively, perhaps easier to compute:\n\n935,817 + 992,625:\n\nAdding the two numbers:\n\nLet me do 935,817 + 992,625:\n\nStart with 900,000 + 900,000 = 1,800,000.\n\nThen 35,817 + 92,625:\n\n35,817 + 92,625:\n\n35,000 +92,000 =127,000\n\n817 +625 =1,442\n\nTotal: 127,000 +1,442 =128,442\n\nSo total sum: 1,800,000 +128,442 =1,928,442. Yes, matches. So the answer is correct.\n\nTherefore, the reasoning steps are as above. I think that's thorough.\n</think>\n\n",
