gits would be:\n\nHundred thousands: 6\n\nTen thousands: 7 (from 5+2)\n\nThousands: 7 (from 7+0)\n\nHundreds: 7 (from 4+2 + 1)\n\nTens: 1 (from 11 in the tens place, with the 1 carried over)\n\nOnes: 6\n\nSo the number would be 6 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 6 (ones). So combining those: 677,716. Wait, but let me confirm by adding the numbers another way.\n\nAlternatively, maybe adding the numbers as whole numbers:\n\n457,456 + 220,260.\n\nLet me add 457,456 + 200,000 = 657,456.\n\nThen add 20,260: 657,456 + 20,000 = 677,456. Then add 260: 677,456 + 260 = 677,716. Okay, that matches. So the answer is indeed 677,716. I think my initial calculation was right, but I just wanted to double-check to be sure. Maybe I confused the place names earlier but the digits add up correctly. Alright, so the final answer should be 677,716.\n</think>\n\n",
