thousands:0\n\nThousands:9\n\nHundreds:3\n\nTens:7\n\nOnes:3\n\nSo that would be 609,373. Hmm, but when I add the two numbers:\n\n109,652 + 499,721. Let me add them another way to confirm.\n\nAlternatively, 109,652 + 499,721:\n\nAdding the two numbers:\n\nLet me try adding 100,000 + 400,000 = 500,000.\n\nThen 9,000 + 99,000 (wait, no, let's break down properly):\n\nWait maybe better to do the addition step by step again.\n\nFirst number: 109652.\n\nSecond number: 499721.\n\nAdding:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 2 +1 =3.\n\nTens:5+2=7.\n\nHundreds:6+7=13. Write 3, carryover 1.\n\nThousands:9 (from first number's thousands digit, which is the fourth digit from right, since 109,652 is 1 0 9 6 5 2? Wait, maybe I messed up the place breakdown earlier. Wait, perhaps my confusion is in the place names. Let's clarify the digit positions.\n\nWait, let me write the numbers with their digits clearly separated:\n\n109,652 is:\n\nDigit positions (from right, starting at 1):\n\n1: Ones: 2\n\n2: Tens: 5\n\n3: Hundreds: 6\n\n4: Thousands: 9\n\n5: Ten-thousands: 0\n\n6: Hundred-thousands: 1\n\nSimilarly, 499,721:\n\n1: Ones:1\n\n2: Tens:2\n\n3: Hundreds:7\n\n4: Thousands:9\n\n5: Ten-thousands:9\n\n6: Hundred-thousands:4\n\nSo when adding:\n\nPosition 1: 2+1=3\n\nPosition 2:5+2=7\n\nPosition 3:6+7=13 \u2192 3 with carryover 1\n\nPosition 4:9+9 +1 (carryover) = 19 \u2192 9 with carryover 1\n\nPosition5:0 +9 +1 (carryover) =10 \u2192 0 with carryover 1\n\nPosition6:1 +4 +1 (carryover) =6 \u2192 6 with no carryover.\n\nThus, the digits from position 1 to 6 are: 3,7,3,9,0,6 \u2192 which is 609,373. Hmm, so that seems correct. Wait, but maybe I should do the addition another way to cross-verify.\n\nLet me compute 109,652 + 499,721 using another method. Let's break down the numbers:\n\n109,652 is 100,000 + 9,000 + 600 +50 +2.\n\n499,721 is 400,000 + 99,000 + 700 +20 +1.\n\nAdding them together:\n\n100,000 +400,000 =500,000.\n\n9,000 +99,000 =108,000.\n\n600+700=1,300.\n\n50+20=70.\n\n2+1=3.\n\nNow add all those:\n\n500,000 +108,000 =608,000.\n\n608,000 +1,300 =609,300.\n\n609,300 +70 =609,370.\n\n609,370 +3 =609,373. Okay, so that confirms it again. So the answer is indeed 609,373. Therefore, the reasoning steps are correct. I think that's solid. Maybe I was just second-guessing myself, but the cross-verification worked. So the final answer should be 609,373.\n</think>\n\n",
