or-like addition:\n\n121,363 + 947,525.\n\nAdding the two numbers:\n\n121,363\n\n+947,525\n\n------------\n\nLet me add the numbers step by step:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n3 +5 =8 (ones)\n\n6 +2 =8 (tens)\n\n3 +5 =8 (hundreds)\n\n1 (from first number's thousands) +7 (from second's thousands) =8 (thousands)\n\n2 (ten thousands) +4 (ten thousands) =6 (ten thousands)\n\n1 (hundred thousands) +9 (hundred thousands) =10, which is 0 in hundred thousands and carryover 1 to millions, which gives 1 in millions place.\n\nSo combining all: 1,068,888. That's the same as before. \n\nWait, but I just want to make sure that the places are correctly aligned. Let me check the number of digits:\n\n121,363 has 6 digits, 947,525 also has 6 digits. When adding, the sum can have up to 7 digits. Since the highest place was hundred thousands for both, their sum's highest place is millions.\n\nYes, so the result is 1,068,888. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can do this addition in parts. For example, 121,363 + 900,000 = 1,021,363. Then adding the remaining 47,525:\n\n1,021,363 +47,525 = ?\n\n1,021,363 +40,000 =1,061,363\n\n1,061,363 +7,525 = 1,068,888. \n\nSame result. Okay, so I think that's correct. \n\nTherefore, the final answer should be 1,068,888.\n"]
