s from right: ones (6), tens (2), hundreds (6), thousands (6), ten thousands (9), hundred thousands (9).\n\nSo thousands place in first number: 6 (fourth digit from right).\n\nSecond number 276,139:.\n\nDigits from right: ones (9), tens (3), hundreds (1), thousands (6), ten thousands (7), hundred thousands (2).\n\nSo thousands place in second number is 6. Therefore 6 + 6 = 12. So write 2, carryover 1.\n\nMoving to ten thousands place: 9 (from first number) + 7 (from second) = 16, plus the carried 1 is 17. So write 7, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands place: 9 (first) + 2 (second) = 11, plus the carried 1 is 12. So write 2 and carryover 1. But since there are no more digits, that 1 becomes a new digit at the start.\n\nPutting it all together:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 5.\n\nTens:6.\n\nHundreds:7.\n\nThousands:2 (with carryover).\n\nThen ten thousands place became 7 (after carryover), and hundred thousands place is 2 with a carryover 1, so the final digit is 1 in the millions place.\n\nSo combining all digits:.\n\n1 (million) 2 (hundred thousand) 7 (ten thousand) 2 (thousand) 7 (hundred) 6 (ten) 5 (one).\n\nWait, let me check the step-by-step again to make sure:.\n\nLet me write the addition step by step:.\n\n          996626.\n        + 276139.\n        -----------.\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 6+9=15 → 5, carry 1.\n\nTens: 2+3=5 +1=6 → 6, no carry.\n\nHundreds:6+1=7 →7.\n\nThousands:6 (from first) +6 (from second)=12 → 2, carry 1.\n\nTen thousands:9 (first) +7 (second)=16 +1=17 →7, carry 1.\n\nHundred thousands:9+2=11 +1=12 → 2, carry 1.\n\nThen the carried 1 becomes the millions place. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
