usands), 1 (ten thousands), 1 (hundred thousands).\n\nSo when adding thousands place: the first number has 3 (thousands place) and the second has 3 (thousands place). So 3+3=6 plus the carried 1 makes 7. Correct.\n\nTen thousands place: 8 (from first number) +1 (from second) =9. .\n\nHundred thousands place: 8 +1=9. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
