reds:4+2=6 plus 1 carried over makes 7. Write 7, no carryover.\n\nThousands:1+0=1. Write 1, no carryover.\n\nTen thousands place:7 (from first number\'s ten thousands) +8 (from second\'s ten thousands)=15. So write 5, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands place:7 (first\'s hundred thousands) +7 (second\'s hundred thousands)=14, plus the carried over 1 makes 15. So here, we write 5 in the hundred thousands place and carryover 1 to the millions place.\n\nMillions place: 0+0 plus the carried over 1 gives 1.\n\nSo putting all digits together from right to left:\n\nOnes:9, Tens:1, Hundreds:7, Thousands:1, Ten thousands:5, Hundred thousands:5, Millions:1.\n\nSo the number is 1,551,719.\n\nWait, let\'s verify with another method. Let me add the numbers in parts.\n\n771,461 + 780,258.\n\nBreaking them into thousands:\n\n771,461 = 700,000 + 70,000 + 1,000 + 400 + 60 +1.\n\n780,258 = 700,000 + 80,000 + 0 + 200 + 50 +8.\n\nAdding each part:\n\n700,000 +700,000 =1,400,000.\n\n70,000 +80,000=150,000.\n\n1,000 +0=1,000.\n\n400+200=600.\n\n60+50=110.\n\n1+8=9.\n\nNow summing all these:\n\n1,400,000 +150,000 =1,550,000.\n\n1,550,000 +1,000=1,551,000.\n\n1,551,000 +600=1,551,600.\n\n1,551,600 +110=1,551,710.\n\n1,551,710 +9=1,551,719.\n\nYes, same result. So the answer should be 1,551,719.\n\nWait but in the initial digit-by-digit addition, the steps led to that. So the final answer is correct.\n\nTherefore, the sum of 771,461 and 780,258 is 1,551,719.\n\nWait but let me check once more with another method, perhaps using rounding:\n\n771,461 + 780,258.\n\nApproximate to nearest thousand:\n\n771,000 +780,000=1,551,000. The actual numbers are 461 more than 771,000 and 258 more than 780,000. So total extra is 461 +258=719. So total is 1,551,000 +719=1,551,719. That matches.\n\nOkay, that\'s consistent. So confident the answer is correct.\n\nNow, to fill in the template. The problem asks for the sum of 771461 and 780258. The reasoning should walk through each digit step by step as per the t