 position to make sure I didn't mix up any places.\n\nWait, maybe I should write each step more carefully. Let me list each digit's place:.\n\nNumbers:.\n880,924: digits are 8 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 4 (ones).\n719,326: digits are 7 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 6 (ones).\n\nAdding each column from right to left:.\n\nOnes: 4 +6 =10 → 0, carryover 1.\nTens: 2 +2 =4 +1=5 →5, no carryover.\nHundreds:9+3=12 →2, carryover 1.\nThousands:0+9=9 +1=10 →0, carryover1.\nTen thousands:8+1=9 +1=10 →0, carryover1.\nHundred thousands:8+7=15 +1=16 →6, carryover1.\n\nWait, but the hundred thousands place addition is 8+7 plus the carryover 1, so total 16. So the digits would be 1 (carryover to millions place), then 6 in hundred thousands, then the rest. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
