e write 2 in the hundred thousands place and carry over 1 to the millions place. Since there are no more digits, that 1 becomes a million. So the total would be 1,227,028?.\n\nWait let me check again step by step:.\n\nLet me align them properly:.\n\n      551067.\n    + 675951.\n    -----------.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 7+1=8.\n\nTens: 6+5=11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds: 0+9=9 +1=10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nThousands: 1+5=6 +1=7. Write 7, no carryover.\n\nTen-thousands: 5+7=12. Write 2, carryover 1.\n\nHundred-thousands:5+6=11 +1=12. Write 2, carryover 1.\n\nMillions place: The carryover 1. So total is 1,227,028?.\n\nWait, but adding 551,067 and 675,951. Let me add them another way to verify. Maybe breaking them into parts.\n\n551,067 + 600,000 = 1,151,067. Then add 75,951. 1,151,067 +75,000 = 1,226,067. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
