, then 8,524 more. So 730,000 +8,524 =738,524. So yeah, perhaps splitting it differently.\n\nAlternatively, adding 674,615 +738,524:\n\nLet me add the hundred thousands first. 600,000 +700,000 =1,300,000.\n\nThen the ten thousands:70,000 +30,000=100,000. So 1,300,000 +100,000=1,400,000.\n\nThousands:4,000 +8,000=12,000. 1,400,000 +12,000=1,412,000.\n\nHundreds:600 +500=1,100. Adding that:1,412,000 +1,100=1,413,100.\n\nTens:10 +20=30. So 1,413,100 +30=1,413,130.\n\nOnes:5 +4=9. Total 1,413,139. Yes, same result. Okay, so that's correct. So the answer should be 1,413,139. Alright, so I think the steps are correct. So the reasoning should follow the digit-by-digit addition with the carryovers as I did first.\n"]
