t, add the hundred thousands: 900,000 + 600,000 = 1,500,000.\n\nThen ten thousands: 80,000 + 20,000 = 100,000.\n\nThousands: 7,000 + 9,000 = 16,000.\n\nHundreds: 300 + 800 = 1,100.\n\nTens: 0 + 20 =20.\n\nOnes:2 +8 =10.\n\nNow add all these together:\n\n1,500,000 + 100,000 = 1,600,000.\n\n1,600,000 +16,000 =1,616,000.\n\n1,616,000 +1,100 =1,617,100.\n\n1,617,100 +20 =1,617,120.\n\n1,617,120 +10 =1,617,130. Okay, same result. That's reassuring.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using another method: 987,302 + 629,828.\n\nLet me see if I can compute mentally. Let me round numbers to make it easier? Not sure, but let's see:\n\n987,302 is 1,000,000 minus 12,698.\n\n629,828 is 600,000 + 29,828.\n\nHmm, maybe not helpful. Alternatively, adding 987,302 + 629,828:\n\nAdd 987,302 + 600,000 first = 1,587,302.\n\nThen add 29,828: 1,587,302 +29,828.\n\n1,587,302 +20,000 =1,607,302.\n\nThen +9,828: 1,607,302 +9,828 =1,617,130. Yep, same answer. So that's three different methods leading to the same result. I think that's correct. Therefore, the sum is 1,617,130.\n</think>\n\n",
