\nOnes: 4 + 5 = 9. Write 9.\n\nTens: 9 + 1 = 10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds: 5 + 8 = 13, plus the 1 carried over is 14. Write 4, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place: 8 (from first number) +7 (second number) = 15, plus 1 is 16. Write 6, carryover 1.\n\nTen-thousands place: 8 (first number) +7 (second number) = 15, plus 1 is 16. Write 6, carryover 1.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 3 +7 =10, plus 1 carried over is 11. So write 1 and carryover 1? Wait, but that's the highest place. Wait, so that would make it 1,1. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
