ndred thousands 2+2=4. So yes, all correct.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I can add the numbers using another method. Let's see:\n\n204,857 + 294,936.\n\nBreak them into parts:\n\n200,000 + 4,000 + 800 + 50 +7.\n\n200,000 + 4,000 = 204,000; plus 800 is 204,800; plus 50 is 204,850; plus 7 is 204,857.\n\nSecond number: 200,000 + 90,000 +4,000 +900 +30 +6.\n\n200,000 +90,000 is 290,000; plus 4,000 is 294,000; plus 900 is 294,900; plus 30 is 294,930; plus 6 is 294,936.\n\nNow adding:\n\n204,857 + 294,936.\n\nLet's add the hundred thousands: 200k + 200k = 400k.\n\nThen the ten thousands: 0 +90k =90k.\n\nThousands: 4k +4k=8k.\n\nHundreds:800 +900=1,700.\n\nTens:50 +30=80.\n\nOnes:7+6=13.\n\nAdding all together: 400k +90k =490k; +8k is 498k; +1,700 is 499,700; +80 is 499,780; +13 is 499,793. Yes, same result.\n\nAlright, seems like the correct sum is 499,793. Therefore, the answer should be that.\n\nWait, but let me check once more with another approach, maybe column addition:\n\nLet me write it out vertically:\n\n\u2003204857.\n\n+294936.\n\n------------.\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:7+6=13. Write 3, carryover 1.\n\nTens:5+3=8 +1=9. Write 9, no carryover.\n\nHundreds:8+9=17. Write 7, carryover 1.\n\nThousands:4+4=8 +1=9. Write 9, no carryover.\n\nTen-thousands:0+9=9.\n\nHundred-thousands:2+2=4.\n\nSo combining all digits from right to left: 3,9,7,9,9,4. Wait, no, actually when writing the digits from right to left, the positions are ones, tens, hundreds, thousands, ten thousands, hundred thousands. So the digits would be:\n\nOnes:3,\n\nTens:9,\n\nHundreds:7,\n\nThousands:9,\n\nTen-thousands:9,\n\nHundred-thousands:4.\n\nSo the number is 4 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 3 (ones). So 499,793. Yep, that's correct. Alright, I think that's solid. No mistakes detected in the steps. So the final answer is 499,793.\n\n</think>\n\n",
