00k = 1,200,000.\n\nThen add 95,991 +48,372.\n\n95,991 +48,372: \n\n95,991 +40,000 =135,991\n\n135,991 +8,372 = 144,363.\n\nSo total is 1,200,000 +144,363 =1,344,363. That matches. Okay, so the answer is correct.\n\nWait, but in the step-by-step breakdown, when adding the hundred-thousands place, 8 +4 +1 (carryover) =13, which is 3 in that place and carryover 1 to millions. So the millions place is 1. So the total is indeed 1,344,363. So the reasoning steps are correct.\n\nBut in the initial problem's template, the user wants the reasoning written in the format with each digit place step. Let me structure that properly.\n\nThe ones place: 1 +2=3.\n\nTens place:9+7=16, so 6 with a carryover.\n\nHundreds place:9+3+1=13, so 3 with carryover.\n\nThousands place:5+8+1=14, so 4 with carryover.\n\nTen-thousands place:9+4+1=14, so 4 with carryover.\n\nHundred-thousands place:8+4+1=13, so 3 with carryover to millions.\n\nThen the final carryover gives the 1 in the millions place.\n\nThus, putting it all together gives 1,344,363. So the answer is correct.\n"]
