calculator style:\n\n876,474\n\n+637,395\n\nAdding the numbers:\n\nStart from the right:\n\n4+5=9\n\n7+9=16 (6, carry 1)\n\n4+3 +1=8 (wait, no: hundreds place. Wait the hundreds digits are 4 and 3, plus carryover 1 from the tens place (the 16). So 4+3=7 +1=8. Correct.\n\nThousands place: 6 +7 =13 \u2192 3, carryover1.\n\nTen-thousands place:7 +3=10 +1 carried over is 11 \u2192 1, carryover1.\n\nHundred-thousands:8 +6=14 +1=15 \u21925, carryover1.\n\nMillions:1. So yes, same as before. Okay, confident now.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe final computed sum is \\boxed{1513869}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 876474 and 637395?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n\n1. The ones place: 4 + 5 = 9\n2. The tens place: 7 + 9 = 16 (write down 6, carry over 1)\n3. The hundreds place: 4 + 3 + 1 (carryover) = 8\n4. The thousands place: 6 + 7 = 13 (write down 3, carry over 1)\n5. The ten-thousands place: 7 + 3 + 1 (carryover) = 11 (write down 1, carry over 1)\n6. The hundred-thousands place: 8 + 6 + 1 (carryover) = 15 (write down 5, carry over 1)\n7. The millions place: 1 (carryover)\n\nAnswer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is \\boxed{1513869}.",
