t: 564,616 +36,725.\n\nAdding 564,616 + 30,000 =594,616.\n\nThen +6,725: 594,616 +6,000 =600,616, then +725 =601,341. Okay, that matches. So the answer should be 601,341.\n\nWait, but in the initial breakdown, when I added the ten thousands place, I had 6 (from 364,616's ten thousands place) plus 3 (from 236,725's ten thousands place) which is 9 plus the carryover 1 makes 10. So that gives 0 in that place and carryover 1 to the next. That seems correct. So the digits are 6 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 1 (ones). So 601,341. That's correct.\n\nSo I think that's the right answer. Maybe I was just overthinking, but the steps check out both by column addition and by breaking down the numbers into parts.\n</think>\n\n",
