 (tens), 0 (ones).\n\nSecond number: 946,796 is 9 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 6 (ones).\n\nSo aligning them:.\n\nHundred thousands: 7 + 9 = 16.\n\nTen thousands: 0 + 4 = 4.\n\nThousands: 7 + 6 =13.\n\nHundreds: 1 +7 =8.\n\nTens: 1 +9 =10.\n\nOnes:0 +6=6.\n\nWait, but adding this way might be confusing. Maybe better to do column-wise from right to left as in standard addition.\n\nLet me try again:.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\nOnes: 0 + 6 = 6. Write 6.\n\nTens: 1 + 9 = 10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds: 1 (from first number) +7 (second number) + 1 (carryover) = 9. Write 9, no carryover.\n\nThousands place: 7 (first number) + 6 (second number) =13. Write 3, carryover 1.\n\nTen-thousands place: 0 (first number) +4 (second number) + 1 (carryover) =5. Write 5, no carryover.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 7 (first number) +9 (second number) =16. Write 6, carryover 1. But since there are no more digits, that 1 is added as a new digit at the beginning.\n\nPutting it all together:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes:6.\n\nTens:0.\n\nHundreds:9.\n\nThousands:3 (with carryover 1).\n\nTen-thousands:5.\n\nHundred-thousands:6, plus the carried-over 1 makes 16, so we write 6 and carryover 1, but since that's the highest place, it becomes 1 in the millions place.\n\nWait, let me track each step properly:.\n\nLet me write down each step:.\n\nNumbers:.\n\n     707110.\n   + 946796.\n   -----------.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones):.\n\n1. Ones place: 0 + 6 = 6. Write down 6.\n\n2. Tens place: 1 + 9 = 10. Write 0, carry over 1.\n\n3. Hundreds place: 1 (from first number) + 7 (from second number) + 1 (carryover) = 9. Write 9, no carryover.\n\n4. Thousands place: 7 (first) + 6 (second) = 13. Write 3, carry over 1.\n\n5. Ten-thousands place: 0 (first) + 4 (second) + 1 (carryover) =5. Write 5, no carryover.\n\n6. Hundred-thousands place: 7 (first) + 9 (second) = 16. Write 6, carry over 1.\n\nBut since there are no more digits, that carried over 1 becomes a new digit at the millions place. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
