nd has a 2. Adding those: 9 +2 =11. So that's 1 and 1, meaning 11. So we write 1 in the hundred thousands place and carry over another 1, but since there are no more digits, that 1 becomes a new digit at the beginning. Wait, but actually, both numbers only have up to the hundred thousands place. Wait, 926399 is a six-digit number, so 9 is in the hundred thousands place. The second number is 254,485, which is also six digits, so 2 in the hundred thousands. Adding 9 +2 gives 11, so we write 1 in the hundred thousands place and carry over 1 to the millions place. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
