3\n\nTens:4\n\nOnes:7\n\nSo putting together: 635,347. Wait but let me check with another method to confirm.\n\nAlternatively, maybe adding the numbers as whole numbers:\n\n118,732 + 500,000 is 618,732. Then add 16,615 (since 516,615 -500,000=16,615). So 618,732 +16,615.\n\n618,732 +10,000 = 628,732\n\n628,732 +6,000 = 634,732\n\n634,732 +615 = 635,347. So that matches. So the answer is correct.\n\nWait, but let me do the addition another way, perhaps breaking down each number into its components.\n\n118,732 = 100,000 + 10,000 + 8,000 + 700 + 30 +2\n\n516,615 = 500,000 +10,000 +6,000 +600 +10 +5\n\nAdding them together:\n\n100,000 +500,000 =600,000\n\n10,000 +10,000 =20,000\n\n8,000 +6,000 =14,000\n\n700 +600 =1,300\n\n30 +10 =40\n\n2 +5=7\n\nNow adding all these:\n\n600,000 +20,000 =620,000\n\n620,000 +14,000 =634,000\n\n634,000 +1,300 =635,300\n\n635,300 +40=635,340\n\n635,340 +7=635,347. Yep, same result. So that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is 635,347. I think that's right. Let me just ensure I didn't make a mistake in the digit places when I first did the column addition. The steps there were correct. So the answer should be 635,347.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe sum of 118732 and 516615 is \\boxed{635347}.\n"]
