2 (write 2, carry 1).\nTens:4 +0 +1=5.\nHundreds:3 +0=3.\nThousands:9 +0=9.\nTen thousands:4 +8=12 (write 2, carry 1).\nHundred thousands:6 +7 +1(carry)=14.\n\nWait, so putting it all together:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 2.\nTens:5.\nHundreds:3.\nThousands:9.\nTen thousands:2 (with a carryover).\nHundred thousands:14?.\n\nWait, so the hundred thousands place would be 14? That would actually be 1,4 in the hundred thousands and millions place?.\n\nWait, let me go step by step again carefully.\n\nLet me write each digit column:.\n\nLet me write both numbers with their digits separated:.\n\n649,344: .\n\nDigits from right to left (ones to hundred thousands):.\n\nPosition 1 (ones):4.\n\nPosition 2 (tens):4.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):3.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):9.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):4.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):6.\n\n780,008:.\n\nPosition1 (ones):8.\n\nPosition2 (tens):0.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):0.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):0.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):8.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):7.\n\nPosition7 (millions):0 (since it's a 6-digit number, but the first number is also 6 digits, so the second number has a 7th digit if we consider up to hundred thousands as the sixth. Wait actually, both are 6-digit numbers. Wait 780,008 is 7 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), etc. So both are 6-digit numbers.\n\nWait, adding 649,344 (649344) and 780,008 (780008).\n\nLet me align them properly:.\n\n        649344.\n      +780008.\n      ---------.\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes place: 4 + 8 =12. Write 2, carryover 1.\n\nTens place: 4 +0 +1=5. Write 5, no carryover.\n\nHundreds place:3 +0=3. Write 3.\n\nThousands place:9 +0=9. Write9.\n\nTen thousands place:4 +8=12. Write 2, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands place:6 +7 +1 (carryover)=14. So here, 14. Since this is the hundred thousands place, 14 would mean 4 in the hundred thousands and carryover 1 to the millions place.\n\nBut since there are no higher digits, that carryover becomes a new digit at the millions place.\n\nSo putting all together:.\n\nThe digits from right to left are:.\n\nOnes:2.\n\nTens:5.\n\nHundreds:3.\n\nThousands:9.\n\nTen thousands:2.\n\nHundred thousands:4.\n\nMillions:1 (from the carryover).\n\nSo combining all digits: 1 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands),9 (thousands),3 (hundreds),5 (tens),2 (ones). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
