0,000 + 3,000 + 400 + 80 +2\n\n885,145 = 800,000 +80,000 +5,000 +100 +40 +5\n\nAdding each place:\n\nMillions: 0 +0 =0 (but since the numbers are over 800k, the total might go to 1.7 million)\n\nHundreds of thousands: 800k +800k =1,600,000\n\nTen thousands: 30,000 +80,000 =110,000\n\nThousands:3,000 +5,000 =8,000\n\nHundreds:400 +100 =500\n\nTens:80 +40 =120\n\nOnes:2 +5=7\n\nNow adding all these together:\n\n1,600,000 +110,000 =1,710,000\n\n1,710,000 +8,000 =1,718,000\n\n1,718,000 +500 =1,718,500\n\n1,718,500 +120 =1,718,620\n\n1,718,620 +7 =1,718,627.\n\nOkay, so that matches my previous result. So the total is indeed 1,718,627. So my initial mistake was when I first thought ten thousands place was 8 and 8, but actually, the first number's ten thousands digit is 3 and the second's is 8, leading to 11 there, which caused the carryover. So I need to make sure I align the digits correctly.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer should be 1,718,627.\n"] 60%|#####9    | 299/500 [3:13:15<2:21:00, 42.09s/it]
