m of 927,036 and 320,153 is 1,247,189.\n\nWait, but let me check the problem again to ensure I didn't misread the numbers. The first number is 927036, which is 927,036, and the second is 320,153. Yes. So 927,036 plus 320,153. Yes, that's right.\n\nAnother way: using calculator-like addition:\n\n927036\n\n+320153\n\nAdd each digit:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n6+3=9\n\n3+5=8\n\n0+1=1\n\n7+0=7\n\n2+2=4\n\n9+3=12 (carryover 1, so the 2 is in that place, and the 1 is added to the next higher place, which becomes the millions digit 1.\n\nSo the digits are 1 (millions), 2 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 9 (ones). So 1,247,189. Correct.\n\nAlright, I think that's solid. I don't see any mistakes in the reasoning. All the steps add up. So the final answer should be 1,247,189.\n</think>\n\n",
