sands place?) Wait, let me check the number breakdown again. .\n\nWait, 379,680 is 3 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 0 (ones). .\n\nAnd 482,616 is 4 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 6 (ones). .\n\nWait, so when adding the thousands place: in 379,680, the thousands digit is 9 (since it's 3 (100k), 7 (10k), 9 (thousands)), and in 482,616 it's 2 (since 4 (100k), 8 (10k), 2 (thousands). So 9 + 2 = 11 plus the carried 1 makes 12, so that's correct. .\n\nThen the ten-thousands place: 7 (from first number) and 8 (from second). 7+8=15, plus the carried 1 is 16. So write 6, carryover 1. .\n\nHundred thousands place: 3 +4 =7 plus the carried 1 is 8. .\n\nSo the digits from right to left are 6 (ones), 9 (tens), 2 (hundreds), 2 (thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 8 (hundred thousands). Wait, so putting them together, that would be 862,300? Wait, let's see:.\n\nWait, the digits in order:.\n\nHundred thousands: 8.\n\nTen thousands: 6.\n\nThousands: 2.\n\nHundreds: 2.\n\nTens:9.\n\nOnes:6. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
