 that's 1 in the hundreds place and carryover 1 to the thousands.\n\nWait, but do I add the carryover here? Wait, the previous step (tens) didn't have a carryover. Wait, the previous step had a carryover from the ones, which was added to the tens. Wait, let me go step by step again to make sure.\n\nStarting over, maybe:.\n\nOnes place: 1 + 9 = 10 → 0, carryover 1.\n\nTens place: 2 + 2 = 4, plus carryover 1 → 5. No carryover now.\n\nHundreds place: 3 + 8 = 11. So here, that's 11. So write down 1, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place: The first number has 6, second has 9. 6 + 9 = 15, plus the carryover 1 makes 16. So thousands place is 6, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands place: First number has 5, second has 5. 5 +5 =10, plus carryover 1 is 11. So ten thousands place is 1, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands place: 8 +7 =15, plus carryover 1 →16. So that's 6 in the hundred thousands place and carryover 1. But since there are no more digits, that carryover becomes a new digit at the beginning.\n\nPutting it all together:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 0.\n\nTens:5.\n\nHundreds:1 (with carryover 1 to thousands).\n\nThousands place: 15 +1 (carryover) → 16, so digit is 6, carryover 1.\n\nWait, maybe I need to track each step carefully.\n\nWait, let me write down each digit step by step with the carryover.\n\nLet me structure it properly:.\n\nNumbers aligned:.\n\n\u20038 5 6 3 2 1.\n\n+7 5 9 8 2 9.\n\n------------.\n\nStarting from the right (ones):.\n\n1 + 9 = 10 → 0, carryover 1.\n\nTens: 2 + 2 = 4, plus 1 →5. No carryover.\n\nHundreds: 3 +8 =11 →1, carryover 1.\n\nThousands:6 +9 =15, plus 1 →16 →6, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands:5 +5 =10, plus 1 →11 →1, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands:8 +7 =15, plus 1 →16 →6, carryover 1.\n\nNow, since we're done with all digits, the carryover 1 becomes the next digit (millions place).\n\nSo putting all digits together with the final carryover:.\n\nThe digits from right to left are:.\n\nOnes:0.\n\nTens:5.\n\nHundreds:1.\n\nThousands:6.\n\nTen thousands:1.\n\nHundred thousands:6.\n\nPlus the carryover 1 in the millions place. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
