messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the addition problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of <<number1>> and <<number2>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n1. The ones place: <<digit1>>\n2. The tens place: <<digit2>>\n<<other digits>>\nAnswer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 512727 and 851989?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\nOkay, so I need to add 512,727 and 851,989. Let me start by writing them down one on top of the other, aligning the digits properly. Hmm, let's see:.\n\nFirst, I'll line up the numbers by their place values. Starting from the rightmost digits, which are the ones place. The first number is 512,727. Breaking that down, the digits are 5 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 2 (tens), and 7 (ones). The second number is 851,989, which is 8 (hundred thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 8 (tens), and 9 (ones). .\n\nWait, actually, let me make sure. Let me write them out digit by digit to avoid confusion:.\n\n512727:.\n- Hundred thousands: 5.\n- Ten thousands: 1.\n- Thousands: 2.\n- Hundreds: 7.\n- Tens: 2.\n- Ones: 7.\n\n851989:.\n- Hundred thousands: 8.\n- Ten thousands: 5.\n- Thousands: 1.\n- Hundreds: 9.\n- Tens: 8.\n- Ones: 9.\n\nNow, adding them starting from the ones place. .\n\nOnes place: 7 + 9. That's 16. So I write down 6 and carry over 1 to the tens place.\n\nTens place: 2 + 8 = 10, plus the carried over 1 makes 11. So I write 1 and carry over another 1.\n\nHundreds place: 7 + 9 = 16, plus the carried over 1 gives 17. Write 7, carry over 1.\n\nThousands place: 2 + 1 = 3, plus the 1 carried over is 4. No carryover here.\n\nTen thousands place: 1 + 5 = 6. Since there's no carryover from the thousands, that stays 6.\n\nHundred thousands place: 5 + 8 = 13. .\n\nPutting all together: 13 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 6 (ones). Wait, hold on, let me check again step by step because I might have messed up the places.\n\nWait, maybe I should do it step by step vertically. Let me try again:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes column: 7 + 9 = 16. So 6, carryover 1.\n\nTens column: 2 + 8 = 10, plus 1 is 11. So 1, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds column: 7 + 9 = 16, plus 1 is 17. So 7, carryover 1.\n\nThousands column: 2 (from first number) +1 (from second number) = 3, plus 1 carried over is 4. So 4, no carryover.\n\nTen thousands column: 1 (from first number) +5 (from second) = 6. So 6, no carryover.\n\nHundred thousands column: 5 +8 =13. So 3 in the hundred thousands place and carryover 1 to millions place. Wait, but 5+8 is 13, so actually, the hundred thousands place becomes 3 and we have a 1 in the millions place. .\n\nSo putting it all together, the total sum is 1 (millions) 3 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 6 (ones). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
