ny digits.\n\nWait, let me redo the places carefully:.\n\nLet me write each digit in columns:.\n\n        8 3 7 1 9 1.\n      + 9 1 3 5 2 4.\n      ----------------.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\nOnes: 1 +4 =5.\n\nTens: 9 +2=11 (carry 1, write 1).\n\nHundreds:1 (from first) +5 (second) +1 (carry) =7.\n\nThousands:7 (first) +3 (second) =10 (carry 1, write 0).\n\nTen thousands:3 +1 =4 plus the carryover 1 makes 5.\n\nHundred thousands:8 +9=17 (carryover 1, write 7).\n\nThen the carryover 1 becomes the millions place.\n\nSo the total is 1 (millions), 7 (hundred thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands),7 (hundreds),1 (tens),5 (ones). So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
