ining 66,951: 1,570,156 + 66,951 = 1,637,107. That matches. So that's correct. \n\nAlternatively, maybe adding digit by digit again to confirm:\n\nStarting over:\n\nOnes: 6 +1 =7. \n\nTens:5+5=10 (0, carryover 1)\n\nHundreds:1+9=10 +1=11 (1, carryover 1)\n\nThousands:0+6=6 +1=7 (no carryover)\n\nTen thousands:7+6=13 (3, carryover1)\n\nHundred thousands:7+8=15 +1=16 (6, carryover1)\n\nNow, since there are no more digits, the carryover 1 is added as the next digit (millions place). So the digits from right to left are 7,0,1,7,3,6,1. Wait, no. Wait, when you write the digits, the first digit is millions, then hundred thousands, etc. So the total is 1 (million) 6 (hundred thousand) 3 (ten thousand) 7 (thousand) 1 (hundred) 0 (ten) 7 (one). So yes, 1,637,107. \n\nTherefore, the answer should be correct.\n"]
