k that again.\n\nWait a second, maybe I made a mistake in the thousands place. Let me go through each step again carefully.\n\nStarting over:.\n\nNumbers:.\n\n\u2003409,828.\n+391,160.\n----------.\n\nBreaking it down by place:.\n\nOnes place: 8 + 0 = 8 (correct).\n\nTens place: 2 + 6 = 8 (correct).\n\nHundreds place: 8 + 1 = 9 (correct).\n\nThousands place: 9 (from 409,828) + 1 (from 391,160) = 10. So we write 0 and carry over 1 to the next (ten thousands) place.\n\nTen thousands place: 0 (from first number) + 9 (from second number) + 1 (carryover) = 10. So again, we write 0 here and carry over 1 to the hundred thousands place.\n\nHundred thousands place: 4 + 3 + 1 (carryover) = 8. .\n\nSo putting all the digits together from right to left: .\n\nOnes:8, Tens:8, Hundreds:9, Thousands:0, Ten thousands:0, Hundred thousands:8. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
