rting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 1 +7 =8.\n\nTens:1 +1=2.\n\nHundreds:0 +1=1.\n\nThousands:1 +2=3.\n\nTen thousands:3 +9=12 (so 2 here, carryover 1).\n\nHundred thousands:1 +5 +1(carry)=7.\n\nSo combining all digits: 7 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 8 (ones). Wait, no, wait. Wait, the thousands place was 1+2=3, so thousands digit is 3. Then the ten thousands was 3+9=12, so ten thousands is 2 with carryover. Then the hundred thousands is 1+5+1=7. So, let me directly conclude the answer. The answer is "]]
